# Line endings.
#
# Git stores every text file with LF and checks it out as LF on every OS.
# Without this the repo drifts: a Windows checkout writes CRLF, git compares
# bytes, and every file reports as wholly rewritten. That is what happened
# after the September 2026 restore — ~350 files showed as modified when only
# 11 had real changes, which is a good way to lose work under the noise, or
# to commit a whole-repo whitespace change by reaching for `git commit -a`.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text and leave binaries alone; `eol=lf` pins the
# working-tree ending so this cannot drift back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.mp4   binary
